\ A runtime definition in an AOT binary mints a dispatch id from the process counter. The
\ image loader's dispatch replay registers method entries under freeze-time ids verbatim,
\ and boot must advance the counter past them, or a minted id aliases a replayed generic's
\ identity and the word's introspection lists that generic's methods.
\
\ Sixty ids are minted at runtime, enough to walk any plausible gap between the counter's
\ post-prelude position and the replayed range. The summed method count over the minted
\ words must be zero on every tier. Before the counter advance, the runtime-image
\ interpreter-linked binary printed 2 here: one minted id landed on `poke`'s replayed id
\ and picked up its two methods.
\
\ The definitions arrive through a top-level `eval-string`, which the freeze collects as a plain
\ statement and which defines into the caller's scope. A word body would bracket them in a
\ transient frame of its own, which `>word-info` does not read.

poke: ( value -- string ) generic [ drop "default" ] ;
poke: method{ fixnum } [ drop "fix" ] ;
poke: method{ string } [ drop "str" ] ;

minted: ( -- arr ) const [
  { w0: w1: w2: w3: w4: w5: w6: w7: w8: w9:
    w10: w11: w12: w13: w14: w15: w16: w17: w18: w19:
    w20: w21: w22: w23: w24: w25: w26: w27: w28: w29:
    w30: w31: w32: w33: w34: w35: w36: w37: w38: w39:
    w40: w41: w42: w43: w44: w45: w46: w47: w48: w49:
    w50: w51: w52: w53: w54: w55: w56: w57: w58: w59:
  }
] ;

5 poke print-line

minted [ >string ": ( -- n ) [ 0 ] ; " #append ] #map "" [ #append ] #reduce eval-string

minted [ >word-info methods>> #len ] #map 0 [ + ] #reduce .
